I have a Ultra Enterprise 2 for testing: dual 168 MHz US I, 1G RAM, 1 9G
disk, onboard hme nic, sbus cg6 framebuffer & type 5 keyboard for debugging.


2.4 SMP kernel from Debian runs fine, I can compile kernels, update
debian etc.

2.6 SMP kernel (2.6.6+BK snapshot as of May 21 2004) hangs at random
places:

Usually it starts up, acquires IP via DHCP, starts programs until it
reaches Exim - then hangs hard. It's pingable after dhcp and before
exim.

Sometimes it hangs during dhcp session.

Sometimes it gets up to login prompt, I can log in via ssh and then it
hangs.

It hangs whether or not the keyboard is attached.

I tried turning on different debugging options in kernel hacking menu.
Some didn't compile and some made it hang very early on boot (nothing
seen with -p). These were 2 stack options and spinlock debugging options
- I don't remember which didn't compile and which caused hangs. Anyway,
I got nothing from them (left most of the others still on).

Turning off PREEMPT did not matter.

Turning off SMP cured it - it can dist-upgrade to unstable and compile
kernels.

Turning PREEMPT back on on UP didn't bring the problem back - UP+PREEMPT
works fine (tried simultaneous disk and network load).

So it seems to be SMP. This is my current configuration after all these
tests. Any ideas where to dig further?

